  "question": {
    "text": "Identify the incorrect pair from the following :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Fluorspar- <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Cryolite- <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>AlF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Fluoroapatite- <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>Ca</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>·</mo><msub><mi>CaF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Carnallite- <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KCl</mi><mo>·</mo><msub><mi>MgCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>·</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Fluorine is present mainly as insoluble fluorides (fluorspar <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, cryolite <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>AlF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math> and fluoroapatite <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>Ca</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo> </mo><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><msub><mi>CaF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> ). Sea water contains chlorides, bromides and iodides of sodium, potassium, magnesium and calcium, but is mainly sodium chloride solution (2.5% by mass). The deposits of dried up seas contain these compounds, e.g., sodium chloride and carnallite, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KCl</mi><mo>.</mo><msub><mi>MgCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>.</p>"
